From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenHarmony PC adaptation <noreply@example.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] Use lowercase olm CMake package name

The Conan package that provides libolm is published as olm/3.2.16 and its
CMakeDeps config files are named olm-config.cmake / olm-config-version.cmake,
with the imported target olm::olm (CMakeDeps derives both names from the Conan
package name). Upstream mtxclient asks for the capitalized Olm 3.2.7 config, so
find_package(Olm 3.2.7 REQUIRED) cannot be satisfied by that package and
configuration fails with "Could not find a package configuration file provided
by Olm".

libolm's own CMake install also ships olm-config.cmake (the name is lowercase
since olm 3.2.x), so lowercasing the package and target reference keeps the
build working against a system-wide libolm install as well; this is a naming
portability fix, not a behavioural change.

Only the CMake build system is touched; the meson build already asks for the
capitalized Olm dependency through dependency('Olm', method: 'cmake') and is
not used by this recipe.

Signed-off-by: OpenHarmony PC adaptation <noreply@example.com>
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 9d9f929..dc51387 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -110,8 +110,8 @@ if(USE_BUNDLED_OLM)
 		)
 	FetchContent_MakeAvailable(Olm)
 else()
-	find_package(Olm 3.2.7 REQUIRED)
-	set_package_properties(Olm PROPERTIES
+	find_package(olm 3.2.7 REQUIRED)
+	set_package_properties(olm PROPERTIES
 		DESCRIPTION "An implementation of the Double Ratchet cryptographic ratchet"
 		URL "https://git.matrix.org/git/olm/about/"
 		TYPE REQUIRED
@@ -296,7 +296,7 @@ target_link_libraries(matrix_client
 	PUBLIC
 	OpenSSL::Crypto
 	OpenSSL::SSL
-	Olm::Olm
+	olm::olm
 	nlohmann_json::nlohmann_json)
 
 if(NOT MSVC AND NOT APPLE)
